  {
   "id": "translate",
   "h2": "Translating them",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "facts": [
      "Find the ending first, as before: <em>-t</em> is \"he\", \"she\" or \"it\"; <em>-mus</em> is \"we\".",
      "<em>-unt</em> and <em>-iunt</em> mean \"they\", just like <em>-nt</em>.",
      "Only the spelling changes with the conjugation: <em>trahit</em> is \"he drags\", just as <em>portat</em> is \"he carries\"."
     ]
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "pueri epistulas <u class=\"c\">scrib</u><u class=\"v\">unt</u>.",
      "en": "The boys <b>are writing</b> letters.",
      "note": "<em>-unt</em> is \"they\": 3rd conjugation."
     }
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "ancillae in villa <u class=\"c\">dormi</u><u class=\"v\">unt</u>.",
      "en": "The slave-girls <b>are sleeping</b> in the house.",
      "note": "<em>-iunt</em> is \"they\": 4th conjugation."
     }
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "dominus servum <u class=\"c\">puni</u><u class=\"v\">t</u>.",
      "en": "The master <b>punishes</b> the slave."
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "watch",
   "h2": "Watch out",
   "exam": true,
   "label": "Common mistakes",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "facts": [
      "<em>-unt</em> and <em>-iunt</em> are \"they\": <em>ducunt</em>, \"they lead\"; <em>veniunt</em>, \"they come\".",
      "<em>-es</em> in the 2nd conjugation is \"you\": <em>vides</em>, \"you see\". \"He sees\" is <em>videt</em>.",
      "The first person of the 2nd and 4th ends in <em>-eo</em> and <em>-io</em>: <em>video</em> is \"I see\", and <em>audio</em> is \"I hear\".",
      "A 3rd conjugation <em>-it</em> is \"he\", \"she\" or \"it\": <em>legit</em>, \"he reads\"."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
